{"task_id": "gcd_lcm~d2~1b0da396", "family": "gcd_lcm", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 2, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def gcd_lcm(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int] - return (greatest common divisor, least common multiple) as a tuple. Example: gcd_lcm(4, 6) == (2, 12).\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef gcd_lcm(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    from math import gcd\n    return (gcd(a, b), a * b // gcd(a, b))\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
