{"task_id": "balanced~d3~3df37947", "family": "balanced", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 3, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def balanced(s: str) -> bool - s contains only ( ) [ ] { }; return True exactly when every bracket closes correctly and in the right order. Example: balanced('([{}])') == True, balanced('([)]') == False.\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef balanced(s: str) -> bool:\n    stack = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char in '({[':\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in ')}]':\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            top = stack.pop()\n            if (top == '(' and char == ')') or (top == '[' and char == ']') or (top == '{' and char == '}'):\n                continue\n            else:\n                return False\n    return not stack\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
{"task_id": "rle~d2~0d13cdf9", "family": "rle", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 2, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def rle(s: str) -> list - run-length encode: return a list of (character, run_length) tuples in order. Example: rle('aabb') == [('a', 2), ('b', 2)].\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef rle(s: str) -> list:\n    if not s:\n        return []\n    result = []\n    char = s[0]\n    count = 1\n    for i in range(1, len(s)):\n        if s[i] == char:\n            count += 1\n        else:\n            result.append((char, count))\n            char = s[i]\n            count = 1\n    result.append((char, count))\n    return result\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
{"task_id": "truth_table~d3~08752ea2", "family": "truth_table", "domain": "math", "difficulty": 3, "attempt_kind": "hint", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "How many of the 2^3 possible True/False assignments make this boolean expression True? (NOT binds to the letter after it, XOR is exclusive-or.)\nNOT B\nGive the count as a number.\n\nEnd with your final answer as <answer>...</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To determine how many of the 2^3 = 8 possible True/False assignments make the boolean expression true, we evaluate the expression for each of the 8 combinations of B, C, and D.\n\nThe expression is:\n\n```\nNOT B XOR C XOR D\n```\n\nWe evaluate it for all 8 combinations of B, C, and D:\n\n1. B=False, C=False, D=False → NOT B=True, C=False, D=False → True XOR False XOR False = True\n2. B=False, C=False, D=True → NOT B=True, C=False, D=True → True XOR False XOR True = True\n3. B=False, C=True, D=False → NOT B=True, C=True, D=False → True XOR True XOR False = False\n4. B=False, C=True, D=True → NOT B=True, C=True, D=True → True XOR True XOR True = False\n5. B=True, C=False, D=False → NOT B=False, C=False, D=False → False XOR False XOR False = False\n6. B=True, C=False, D=True → NOT B=False, C=False, D=True → False XOR False XOR True = True\n7. B=True, C=True, D=False → NOT B=False, C=True, D=False → False XOR True XOR False = True\n8. B=True, C=True, D=True → NOT B=False, C=True, D=True → False XOR True XOR True = False\n\nThe number of assignments that make the expression true is 4.\n\n<answer>4</answer>"}]}
