{"task_id": "truth_table~d4~144ef9da", "family": "truth_table", "domain": "math", "difficulty": 4, "attempt_kind": "hint", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "How many of the 2^4 possible True/False assignments make this boolean expression True? (NOT binds to the letter after it, XOR is exclusive-or.)\nNOT B\nGive the count as a number.\n\nEnd with your final answer as <answer>...</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To determine how many of the 2^4 = 16 possible True/False assignments make the boolean expression `NOT B XOR NOT C` true, we evaluate the expression for each of the 16 combinations of B and C.\n\nThe expression is: `NOT B XOR NOT C`.\n\nWe evaluate this for all 16 combinations of B and C:\n\n- B = True, C = True: `NOT B = False`, `NOT C = False`, `False XOR False = False`\n- B = True, C = False: `NOT B = False`, `NOT C = True`, `False XOR True = True`\n- B = False, C = True: `NOT B = True`, `NOT C = False`, `True XOR False = True`\n- B = False, C = False: `NOT B = True`, `NOT C = True`, `True XOR True = False`\n\nThe expression is true for 3 of the 16 combinations.\n\n```python\n# Count how many of the 2^4 possible assignments make the expression true\ncount = 0\nfor b in [True, False]:\n    for c in [True, False]:\n        if not b ^ not c:\n            count += 1\nprint(count)\n```\n\n<answer>8</answer>"}]}
