{"task_id": "max_subarray~d5~2eb070c3", "family": "max_subarray", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 5, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def max_subarray(xs: list[int]) -> int - return the maximum possible sum of a contiguous, non-empty subarray (Kadane). At least one element must be used. Example: max_subarray([1,-2,3]) == 3.\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef max_subarray(xs: list[int]) -> int:\n    max_current = max_global = xs[0]\n    for num in xs[1:]:\n        max_current = max(num, max_current + num)\n        max_global = max(max_global, max_current)\n    return max_global\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
