{"task_id": "base_convert~d2~1699a57e", "family": "base_convert", "domain": "math", "difficulty": 2, "attempt_kind": "hint", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Convert the decimal number 198 to base 4. Give the digits as a plain string (use a-f for 10-15). Example: 26 in base 16 is 1a.\n\nEnd with your final answer as <answer>...</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef decimal_to_base4(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n    digits = []\n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 4\n        if remainder < 10:\n            digits.append(str(remainder))\n        else:\n            digits.append(chr(ord('a') + remainder - 10))\n        n = n // 4\n    return ''.join(reversed(digits))\n\n# Convert 198 to base 4\nresult = decimal_to_base4(198)\nprint(result)\n```\n\n<answer>3012</answer>"}]}
