{"task_id": "linear_solve~d1~343c95a4", "family": "linear_solve", "domain": "math", "difficulty": 1, "attempt_kind": "hint", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Solve for x: 2x + (6) = 28/3. If x is fractional, answer as a reduced fraction p/q. Reduce fully.\n\nEnd with your final answer as <answer>...</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To solve for $ x $ in the equation $ 2x + 6 = \\frac{28}{3} $, we first isolate $ x $:\n\n$$\n2x + 6 = \\frac{28}{3}\n$$\n\nSubtract 6 from both sides:\n\n$$\n2x = \\frac{28}{3} - 6\n$$\n\nConvert 6 to a fraction with denominator 3:\n\n$$\n2x = \\frac{28}{3} - \\frac{18}{3} = \\frac{10}{3}\n$$\n\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{10}{3} \\div 2 = \\frac{10}{6} = \\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nFinal answer:\n\n<answer>5/3</answer>"}]}
{"task_id": "rle~d4~248a5d74", "family": "rle", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 4, "attempt_kind": "hint", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def rle(s: str) -> list - run-length encode: return a list of (character, run_length) tuples in order. Example: rle('aabb') == [('a', 2), ('b', 2)].\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef rle(s: str) -> list:\n    out, i = [], 0\n    while i < len(s):\n        j = i\n        while j < len(s) and s[j] == s[i]: j += 1\n        out.append((s[i], j - i)); i = j\n    return out\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
