{"task_id": "closure~d5~2fd1d9a0", "family": "closure", "domain": "logic", "difficulty": 5, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Facts: N4 > N1; N1 > N3; N4 > N6; N7 > N6; N1 > N5; N2 > N1; N3 > N5. 'Greater-than' is transitive (if A > B and B > C then A > C) and nothing else is true beyond what follows from the facts. Is N2 > N4? Answer yes, no, or unknown (unknown = not determined by the facts).\n\nEnd with your final answer as <answer>...</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\n# Given facts\nfacts = {\n    \"N4 > N1\",\n    \"N1 > N3\",\n    \"N4 > N6\",\n    \"N7 > N6\",\n    \"N1 > N5\",\n    \"N2 > N1\",\n    \"N3 > N5\"\n}\n\n# Check if N2 > N4 can be determined from the facts\n# Use transitivity: If A > B and B > C, then A > C\n# Check if N2 > N4 can be inferred\n\n# Check if N2 > N4 is implied\nif \"N2 > N1\" in facts and \"N1 > N4\" in facts:\n    print(\"yes\")\nelif \"N2 > N1\" in facts and \"N1 > N4\" not in facts:\n    print(\"unknown\")\nelse:\n    print(\"no\")\n\n<answer>unknown</answer>"}]}
{"task_id": "rle~d5~395b477f", "family": "rle", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 5, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def rle(s: str) -> list - run-length encode: return a list of (character, run_length) tuples in order. Example: rle('aabb') == [('a', 2), ('b', 2)].\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef rle(s: str) -> list:\n    if not s:\n        return []\n    result = []\n    current_char = s[0]\n    count = 1\n    for i in range(1, len(s)):\n        if s[i] == current_char:\n            count += 1\n        else:\n            result.append((current_char, count))\n            current_char = s[i]\n            count = 1\n    result.append((current_char, count))\n    return result\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
