{"task_id": "balanced~d5~14aa819d", "family": "balanced", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 5, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def balanced(s: str) -> bool - s contains only ( ) [ ] { }; return True exactly when every bracket closes correctly and in the right order. Example: balanced('([{}])') == True, balanced('([)]') == False.\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef balanced(s: str) -> bool:\n    stack = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char in '({[':\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in ')]}' and len(stack) > 0:\n            top = stack.pop()\n            if (top == '(' and char == ')') or (top == '[' and char == ']') or (top == '{' and char == '}'):\n                continue\n            else:\n                return False\n    return len(stack) == 0\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
