{"task_id": "rle~d5~27332a32", "family": "rle", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 5, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def rle(s: str) -> list - run-length encode: return a list of (character, run_length) tuples in order. Example: rle('aabb') == [('a', 2), ('b', 2)].\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef rle(s: str) -> list:\n    if not s:\n        return []\n    result = []\n    count = 1\n    prev = s[0]\n    for i in range(1, len(s)):\n        if s[i] == prev:\n            count += 1\n        else:\n            result.append((prev, count))\n            prev = s[i]\n            count = 1\n    result.append((prev, count))\n    return result\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
{"task_id": "caesar~d4~06026151", "family": "caesar", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 4, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def caesar(s: str, k: int) -> str - shift each lowercase letter forward by k positions, wrapping around z->a. Non-letters never appear. Example: caesar('abc', 1) == 'bcd'.\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef caesar(s: str, k: int) -> str:\n    result = []\n    for c in s:\n        if c.islower():\n            shifted = ord(c) + k\n            if shifted > ord('z'):\n                shifted = shifted - 26\n            result.append(chr(shifted))\n        else:\n            result.append(c)\n    return ''.join(result)\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
{"task_id": "balanced~d5~06e6f2ed", "family": "balanced", "domain": "code", "difficulty": 5, "attempt_kind": "win", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a precise reasoning assistant. Follow the task's output format exactly: code tasks want a single ```python block defining the required function; other tasks want <answer>...</answer>. No extra prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "def balanced(s: str) -> bool - s contains only ( ) [ ] { }; return True exactly when every bracket closes correctly and in the right order. Example: balanced('([{}])') == True, balanced('([)]') == False.\n\nWrite ONE Python function per the signature below. Standard library only, no input()/print(). Reply with a single ```python code block, then the final word <answer>DONE</answer>. /no_think"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```python\ndef balanced(s: str) -> bool:\n    stack = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char in '({[':\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in ')}]':\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            top = stack.pop()\n            if (top == '(' and char == ')') or (top == '[' and char == ']') or (top == '{' and char == '}'):\n                continue\n            else:\n                return False\n    return not stack\n```\n\n<answer>DONE</answer>"}]}
